  "id": "first-checks",
  "after": "overview",
  "title": "Your first five checks on a new file.",
  "caption": "Before any chart or model, run these five lines of Pandas on your table `df`. They show the size of the table, each column's data type, the blanks, a few real rows and a summary (सारांश, saaraansh) of each number column. Each check can find a problem early, like an age of 999.",
  "alt": "A list of five Pandas checks on a bank's loan file. df.shape gives (5000, 14): rows and columns. df.info() shows that income is stored as text, though it should be a number. df.isna().sum() shows 600 blank incomes, so ask why first. df.head() shows the first 5 rows, to see if they look right. df.describe() shows an age maximum of 999, an error to check. Below: only then, in order, charts of one, two and many columns, then cleaning, then a model or dashboard.",
