  "title": "A one-page data story: finding, chart, action.",
  "caption": "The headline states the finding, not just the topic. The chart is the simplest one for change over time: a line chart, with urban loans for comparison, labelled axes and units. The page ends with one action and a rough ₹ estimate (अंदाज़ा, andaaza): if defaults fall from 8% to 7%, that 1% of ₹50 crore of loans is ₹50 lakh a year. All numbers are made up.",
  "alt": "A mock one-page report. Headline: Rural defaults doubled in two years. A line chart of loans not repaid, in percent, over eight quarters of 2024 and 2025: the rural line rises from 4% to 8%, while the urban line stays near 3%. A green action box: remind rural borrowers 2 weeks before each due date; cutting defaults from 8% to 7% saves ₹50 lakh a year, since 1% of ₹50 crore is ₹50 lakh. A legend: 1, headline is the finding; 2, simplest chart, labelled, with units; 3, one action with a rough rupee sum.",
