 {
  "id": "axis-at-zero",
  "after": "commonMistakes",
  "title": "Start a bar chart's axis at zero.",
  "caption": "The same two pass rates, drawn twice. With the axis starting at 90, school B's bar looks twice as tall as A's, because readers compare bar lengths. Starting at 0 shows the truth: 92.5% and 95% are almost equal. A chart can mislead even when every number on it is correct.",
  "alt": "Two bar charts of the same pass rates, school A 92.5% and school B 95%. Left: the axis starts at 90, so B's bar looks twice as tall as A's; the note says B looks 2 times A. Right: the axis starts at 0, so the bars are almost the same height; the note says almost equal.",
  "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 360 278\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"12\" y=\"6\" width=\"164\" height=\"244\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-surface2\"/><text x=\"22\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-bad\" font-weight=\"700\">Axis starts at 90</text><line x1=\"48\" y1=\"196\" x2=\"166\" y2=\"196\" class=\"s-line\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"43\" y=\"200.5\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\" text-anchor=\"end\">90</text><line x1=\"48\" y1=\"146.7\" x2=\"166\" y2=\"146.7\" class=\"s-line\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"43\" y=\"151.2\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\" text-anchor=\"end\">92</text><line x1=\"48\" y1=\"97.3\" x2=\"166\" y2=\"97.3\" class=\"s-line\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"43\" y=\"101.8\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\" text-anchor=\"end\">94</text><line x1=\"48\" y1=\"48\" x2=\"166\" y2=\"48\" class=\"s-line\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"43\" y=\"52.5\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\" text-anchor=\"end\">96</text><rect x=\"64\" y=\"134.3\" width=\"34\" height=\"61.7\" rx=\"2\" class=\"f-s1\"/><text x=\"81\" y=\"213\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">A</text><rect x=\"116\" y=\"72.7\" width=\"34\" height=\"123.3\" rx=\"2\" class=\"f-s1\"/><text x=\"133\" y=\"213\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">B</text><line x1=\"48\" y1=\"196\" x2=\"166\" y2=\"196\" class=\"s-muted\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"94\" y=\"238\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">B looks 2 × A</text><rect x=\"184\" y=\"6\" width=\"164\" height=\"244\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-surface2\"/><text x=\"194\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-ok\" font-weight=\"700\">Axis starts at 0</text><line x1=\"220\" y1=\"196\" x2=\"338\" y2=\"196\" class=\"s-line\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"215\" y=\"200.5\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\" text-anchor=\"end\">0</text><line x1=\"220\" y1=\"159\" x2=\"338\" y2=\"159\" class=\"s-line\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"215\" y=\"163.5\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\" text-anchor=\"end\">25</text><line x1=\"220\" y1=\"122\" x2=\"338\" y2=\"122\" class=\"s-line\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"215\" y=\"126.5\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\" text-anchor=\"end\">50</text><line x1=\"220\" y1=\"85\" x2=\"338\" y2=\"85\" class=\"s-line\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"215\" y=\"89.5\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\" text-anchor=\"end\">75</text><line x1=\"220\" y1=\"48\" x2=\"338\" y2=\"48\" class=\"s-line\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"215\" y=\"52.5\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\" text-anchor=\"end\">100</text><rect x=\"236\" y=\"59.1\" width=\"34\" height=\"136.9\" rx=\"2\" class=\"f-s1\"/><text x=\"253\" y=\"213\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">A</text><rect x=\"288\" y=\"55.4\" width=\"34\" height=\"140.6\" rx=\"2\" class=\"f-s1\"/><text x=\"305\" y=\"213\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">B</text><line x1=\"220\" y1=\"196\" x2=\"338\" y2=\"196\" class=\"s-muted\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"266\" y=\"238\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Almost equal</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\">Pass rates: school A 92.5%, school B 95%.</text></svg>"
 },
 {
  "id": "simpsons-paradox",
  "after": "commonMistakes",
  "title": "Better in every group, worse overall.",
  "caption": "Centre B has the higher pass rate for strong students (95% against 90%) and for weak students (60% against 50%). Yet overall, A looks better: 82% against 67%. The hidden reason is the mix: B teaches 800 weak students, A only 200. This flip is called Simpson's paradox.",
  "alt": "Horizontal bars for two coaching centres. Strong students: A 90%, 720 of 800; B 95%, 190 of 200; B better. Weak students: A 50%, 100 of 200; B 60%, 480 of 800; B better. All students, in a box: A 82%, 820 of 1,000; B 67%, 670 of 1,000; A looks better. Notes: B takes 800 weak students and A takes 200, so compare inside each group first. Made-up numbers.",
  "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 360 396\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><text x=\"12\" y=\"18\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\" font-weight=\"700\">Pass rates of two coaching centres</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"44\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\">Strong students</text><text x=\"348\" y=\"44\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-ok\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"700\">B better</text><text x=\"14\" y=\"71\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\">A</text><rect x=\"32\" y=\"54\" width=\"171\" height=\"24\" rx=\"3\" class=\"f-s1\"/><text x=\"209\" y=\"71\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\">90%</text><text x=\"348\" y=\"71\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\" text-anchor=\"end\">720 of 800</text><text x=\"14\" y=\"101\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\">B</text><rect x=\"32\" y=\"84\" width=\"180.5\" height=\"24\" rx=\"3\" class=\"f-s2\"/><text x=\"218.5\" y=\"101\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\">95%</text><text x=\"348\" y=\"101\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\" text-anchor=\"end\">190 of 200</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"148\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\">Weak students</text><text x=\"348\" y=\"148\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-ok\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"700\">B better</text><text x=\"14\" y=\"175\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\">A</text><rect x=\"32\" y=\"158\" width=\"95\" height=\"24\" rx=\"3\" class=\"f-s1\"/><text x=\"133\" y=\"175\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\">50%</text><text x=\"348\" y=\"175\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\" text-anchor=\"end\">100 of 200</text><text x=\"14\" y=\"205\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\">B</text><rect x=\"32\" y=\"188\" width=\"114\" height=\"24\" rx=\"3\" class=\"f-s2\"/><text x=\"152\" y=\"205\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\">60%</text><text x=\"348\" y=\"205\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\" text-anchor=\"end\">480 of 800</text><rect x=\"6\" y=\"232\" width=\"348\" height=\"96\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-none s-ink\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"12\" y=\"252\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\">All students</text><text x=\"348\" y=\"252\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-bad\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"700\">A looks better</text><text x=\"14\" y=\"279\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\">A</text><rect x=\"32\" y=\"262\" width=\"155.8\" height=\"24\" rx=\"3\" class=\"f-s1\"/><text x=\"193.8\" y=\"279\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\">82%</text><text x=\"348\" y=\"279\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\" text-anchor=\"end\">820 of 1,000</text><text x=\"14\" y=\"309\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\">B</text><rect x=\"32\" y=\"292\" width=\"127.3\" height=\"24\" rx=\"3\" class=\"f-s2\"/><text x=\"165.3\" y=\"309\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\">67%</text><text x=\"348\" y=\"309\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\" text-anchor=\"end\">670 of 1,000</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"346\" font-size=\"13\">B takes 800 weak students; A takes 200.</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"366\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\">Compare inside each group first.</text><text x=\"348\" y=\"390\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\" text-anchor=\"end\">Made-up numbers</text></svg>"
 },
 {
  "id": "two-tools-one-answer",
  "after": "selfCheck",
  "title": "Same question, two tools, same answer.",
  "caption": "Pandas `groupby` and SQL GROUP BY should give the same city totals from the same five orders. Matching numbers are a cross-check (मिलान, milaan) on your work. If they differ, one of the two has a mistake, often blanks, repeated rows, or one city spelt two ways.",
  "alt": "A small orders table with five rows: Indore 1,200, Bhopal 800, Indore 300, Gwalior 900 and Bhopal 400, and the question: what is the total sales of each city? Below, the Pandas code df.groupby('city')['amount'].sum() and the SQL code SELECT city, SUM(amount) FROM orders GROUP BY city. Both give Bhopal 1,200, Gwalior 900 and Indore 1,500. A green box: same numbers, so you can trust them; if different, look for blanks and repeats.",
  "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 360 440\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><text x=\"12\" y=\"18\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\">orders</text><text x=\"176\" y=\"18\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\">Question:</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"26\" width=\"150\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" class=\"f-surface2 s-line\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"42\" font-size=\"13\">Indore</text><text x=\"154\" y=\"42\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"end\">1,200</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"50\" width=\"150\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" class=\"f-surface2 s-line\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"13\">Bhopal</text><text x=\"154\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"end\">800</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"74\" width=\"150\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" class=\"f-surface2 s-line\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"90\" font-size=\"13\">Indore</text><text x=\"154\" y=\"90\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"end\">300</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"98\" width=\"150\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" class=\"f-surface2 s-line\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"114\" font-size=\"13\">Gwalior</text><text x=\"154\" y=\"114\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"end\">900</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"122\" width=\"150\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" class=\"f-surface2 s-line\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"13\">Bhopal</text><text x=\"154\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"end\">400</text><text x=\"176\" y=\"42\" font-size=\"13\">What is the total</text><text x=\"176\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"13\">sales of each city?</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"160\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\" font-weight=\"700\">Pandas</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"168\" width=\"336\" height=\"30\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f-indigo-soft s-indigo\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"188\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"mono\" style=\"font-size:13px\">df.groupby('city')['amount'].sum()</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"216\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\" font-weight=\"700\">SQL</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"224\" width=\"336\" height=\"48\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f-indigo-soft s-indigo\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"244\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"mono\" style=\"font-size:13px\">SELECT city, SUM(amount) FROM orders</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"262\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"mono\" style=\"font-size:13px\">GROUP BY city;</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\" font-weight=\"700\">Pandas gives</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"298\" width=\"164\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" class=\"f-surface2 s-line\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"314\" font-size=\"13\">Bhopal</text><text x=\"168\" y=\"314\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"700\">1,200</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"322\" width=\"164\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" class=\"f-surface2 s-line\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"338\" font-size=\"13\">Gwalior</text><text x=\"168\" y=\"338\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"700\">900</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"346\" width=\"164\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" class=\"f-surface2 s-line\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"362\" font-size=\"13\">Indore</text><text x=\"168\" y=\"362\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"700\">1,500</text><text x=\"184\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\" font-weight=\"700\">SQL gives</text><rect x=\"184\" y=\"298\" width=\"164\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" class=\"f-surface2 s-line\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"192\" y=\"314\" font-size=\"13\">Bhopal</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"314\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"700\">1,200</text><rect x=\"184\" y=\"322\" width=\"164\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" class=\"f-surface2 s-line\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"192\" y=\"338\" font-size=\"13\">Gwalior</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"338\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"700\">900</text><rect x=\"184\" y=\"346\" width=\"164\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" class=\"f-surface2 s-line\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"192\" y=\"362\" font-size=\"13\">Indore</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"362\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"700\">1,500</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"378\" width=\"336\" height=\"54\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-ok-soft s-ok\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"22\" y=\"400\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\">Same numbers: you can trust them.</text><text x=\"22\" y=\"420\" font-size=\"13\">Different? Look for blanks and repeats.</text></svg>"
 }
